/-!
# Smoothness, free differentials and regularity in characteristic zero

Proof of Stacks 00TX. Let `k` be a field of characteristic `0`, let `S` be a finite type
`k`-algebra, let `𝔮 ⊆ S` be a prime and write `R = S_𝔮` for the local ring, with maximal ideal `𝔪`
and residue field `κ`. Then `S` is smooth at `𝔮` over `k`, the `R`-module `Ω_{R/k}` is free, and
`R` is regular are equivalent.

In characteristic `0` every field extension is separable, so `(1) ↔ (3)` is Lemma 00TV applied to
`κ/k`, and `(1) → (2)` because a formally smooth algebra has projective — hence, over a local ring,
free — differentials. The content is `(2) → (3)`, an induction on `rank_R Ω_{R/k}`. If `𝔪 = 0` then
`R` is a field and regular. Otherwise `𝔪 ≠ 𝔪²` by Nakayama, so some `f ∈ 𝔪` has nonzero class in
`𝔪/𝔪²`, and by Lemma 00TU the element `1 ⊗ df` of `κ ⊗_R Ω_{R/k}` is nonzero. A free module over a
local ring has a functional taking the value `1` at any element that survives in the fibre, so
there is `φ : Ω_{R/k} → R` with `φ(df) = 1`; then `φ ∘ d` is a `k`-derivation of `R` sending `f` to
`1`, which forces `f` to be a nonzerodivisor (Lemma 00TW, where characteristic `0` enters).
The conormal sequence `(f)/(f²) → Ω_{R/k} ⊗_R R/fR → Ω_{(R/fR)/k} → 0` of Lemma 00RU identifies
`Ω_{(R/fR)/k}` with the fibre `R/fR ⊗_R Ω_{R/k}` modulo the line spanned by `1 ⊗ df`, and the base
change of `φ` splits that line off, so `Ω_{(R/fR)/k}` is free of rank one less. Thus `R/fR` is
regular by induction, and `R` is regular by Lemma 00NU.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Smooth.CharZeroRegularity.solution`: the statement of Stacks 00TX, namely
  `Algebra.isSmoothAt_tfae_free_kaehlerDifferential_isRegularLocalRing`.

## Implementation notes

The induction runs over an arbitrary local `k`-algebra `R` in a fixed universe together with a
*fixed* field `κ` and a surjection `R → κ`, rather than over `IsLocalRing.ResidueField R`: the
successive quotients `R/fR` all have the same residue field, so keeping it as a parameter avoids
transporting `Algebra.EssFiniteType k κ` along an isomorphism at each step. The parameter is what
Lemma 00TU asks for anyway, that lemma being stated for an arbitrary surjection onto a field.

The steps of the source's argument that are not tags of the Stacks Project and not in Mathlib are
private lemmas here, each stated for an arbitrary index rather than for the ring at hand.

* Where characteristic zero enters, Stacks 00TW (2): `isUnit_natCast_add_one`, that `n + 1` is
  invertible in an algebra over a field of characteristic zero;
  `mem_span_singleton_pow_succ_of_derivation_apply_eq_one`, the cancellation obtained by
  differentiating `f ^ (n + 1) * b = 0` and dividing by `n + 1`; and
  `mem_nonZeroDivisors_of_derivation_apply_eq_one`, where the Krull intersection theorem turns the
  resulting descent into `⋂ (f) ^ n = 0`.
* The source's two appeals to Nakayama, Lemma 00DV: `exists_mem_maximalIdeal_notMem_sq`, that
  `𝔪 ≠ 𝔪²` when `𝔪 ≠ 0`, and `exists_apply_eq_one_of_tmul_ne_zero`, that an element of a finite
  free module over a local ring surviving in the fibre is the value `1` of some functional.
* The linear algebra of the induction step, over an arbitrary local ring:
  `isCompl_span_singleton_ker`, that a functional taking the value `1` at `x` splits `R ∙ x` off
  as a direct summand, and `free_and_finrank_quotient_span_singleton_of_apply_eq_one`, that
  `M ⧸ R ∙ x` is then free of rank one less.
* The differentials of a quotient: `Ideal.span_toCotangent_eq_top`, that the conormal module of a
  principal ideal is generated by the class of the generator, and
  `KaehlerDifferential.ker_mapBaseChange_quotient`, which combines it with the exactness of
  Stacks 00RU to identify the kernel of `R/I ⊗ Ω_{R/k} → Ω_{(R/I)/k}` for `I = (f)` with the line
  spanned by `1 ⊗ df`. This is the statement that owns the hard part of `(2) → (3)`;
  `KaehlerDifferential.finite_quotient` and
  `free_and_finrank_kaehlerDifferential_quotient_span_singleton` read off from it that
  `Ω_{(R/fR)/k}` is finite free of rank one less.
* Stacks 00NU: `Ideal.eq_of_map_quotientMk_eq`, the ideal correspondence for a quotient, and
  `Ideal.spanFinrank_le_spanFinrank_map_quotient_add_one`, that `f` together with lifts of a
  minimal system of generators of `J/(f)` generates `J`; with the Krull dimension dropping by one,
  these give `isRegularLocalRing_of_isRegularLocalRing_quotient_span_singleton`.
* `Algebra.isSeparableExtension_of_perfectField`, that every extension of a perfect field is
  separable in the sense of Definition 030O (2).

## References

* [Stacks 00TX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00TX)
